# L §2.4 "The loader accepts any spacing that the grammar allows", §2.3 parse rule 3 (a word right after . is a
# field; tally 2.1.6, issue #81): r .n and r. m read as r.n and r.m, and print so. tally 2.1.5's refcore read a
# field's . only touching the token before it (LOAD-PARSE expected end of line, got .); the M0 engine too.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def y: int = r .n + r. m
=== expect
